`allow.hosts` contains `https://api.example.com`. A scheme is not part of a host; the egress proxy matches hostnames, and a reader that strips the scheme and one that refuses it would grant different things. SPEC §4.4: a host is a lower-case DNS name, an IPv4 literal or `localhost`, with an optional single leading `*.` label, or the bare `*`; two implementations must not disagree about what a host entry names.
